Gemini sporadically ends valid tool-calling turns with `MALFORMED_FUNCTION_CALL` or `UNEXPECTED_TOOL_CALL`, and Google Interactions streams can drop before `interaction.completed` or fail with matching malformed tool-call codes. Unlike `MALFORMED_RESPONSE`, those paths were not marked `incomplete-stream`, causing immediate 0-retry failures on recoverable model glitches and 10x retries on blocked Interactions responses.

I moved both protocols onto `incomplete-stream` directly inside their own stream parsers:

- `packages/ai/src/protocols/gemini.ts`: add `MALFORMED_FUNCTION_CALL` and `UNEXPECTED_TOOL_CALL` alongside `MALFORMED_RESPONSE` as `InvalidProviderOutputError({ classification: "incomplete-stream" })`, and ignore non-terminal `FINISH_REASON_UNSPECIFIED`.
- `packages/ai/src/protocols/google-interactions.ts`: drop the custom `onHalt` override so `requireTerminalEvent` marks premature EOF as `incomplete-stream`, normalize `completed` with `function_call` steps to `"tool-calls"`, and classify Interactions stop/block error codes locally via `GeminiGenerateContent.contentFiltered` before falling back to `classifyProviderFailure`.

### Verification

- `bun run typecheck:tsc` and `bun test` in `packages/ai` (1995 passed)
- `bun run check` (35/35 workspace packages passed)

