## What Problem This Solves

`openshell worker run --target-file` opens the selected pairing-target file before checking its type. A FIFO with no writer blocks in `open()` indefinitely, so the regular-file check and worker startup error handling never run.

## User Impact

Pipe-backed targets now fail normally before provider attachment, with guidance to use a readable regular file of at most 64KiB. Regular files, symlinks to regular files, hard links and retry after correcting the path retain their existing behavior. The locally selected target file remains intact.

## Why This Change Was Made

Use the existing SDK `readRegularFile` after resolving the operator-selected link, matching the regular-file admission pattern already used by the connect CLI. Keep the existing 64KiB cap and readiness ordering. Remove the hand-written open/stat/read/close sequence that cannot safely inspect a FIFO after a blocking open.

The owner-level change covers both `run` and its `launch` alias. It introduces no configuration, permission, provider, protocol or storage contract. The empty/oversized/directory assertions extend an existing test; real FIFO process proof stays in the reproducible evidence below rather than adding permanent subprocess tests.

## Evidence

- Scenario: OpenShell worker refuses pipe-backed pairing targets without blocking before provider attachment; Regular files and selected links retain the existing size, readiness, and retained-file contracts
- Entry: node dist/entry.js openshell worker run proof-worker --target-file "$TARGET_FILE" in isolated Linux Node 24.22.1 home, state, workspace and config; disputed owner ran unmocked: extensions/openshell/src/worker-cli.ts readPairingTarget ran unmocked through the real CLI and plugin loader; provider attachment alone uses a local refusing executable fixture
- Same command on base `5e407f5` and head `5390aa2`: `node dist/entry.js openshell worker run proof-worker --target-file "$TARGET_FILE"`
  - Before (base): RED FIFO and FIFO-symlink calls each hit the 20-second guard and receive SIGKILL; neither reaches provider attachment
  - After (head): GREEN the same two calls exit 1 normally in 5761ms and 5845ms with readable-regular-file and existing 64KiB guidance; the process guard never fires
- Readback (subprocess,disk,config-file): Read the actual target and config from disk after all calls, compare bytes, and lstat the original link/FIFO. Both runs retain target SHA256 43f4b89579254eac7829b6d52b09f8c4fc45d111105424d15a97d31f9402cdc8; real fixture log records each attempted provider attachment
- Proof harness: Identical frozen driver SHA256 3729ff92542fe2605fb560bd183cc4db409d7ee48a8e482c35407644b90f6e90; each build-info commit equals its source HEAD; RED 2026-10-31T02:33:41.394Z, GREEN 2026-10-31T03:01:44.950Z
- Control: Across both runs, all four special-file calls make 0 provider calls; four regular/symlink/hardlink/retry calls each make 1 attachment attempt and stop at the pre-existing readiness error, starting 0 nodes. Head FIFO timeout count is 0 versus 2 on base. Config/target byte changes are 0; no pairing-target contents appear in transport argv
- Other callers checked: Full worker CLI/register owner, create/run/launch callers, worker bootstrap and launch owners, core connect CLI regular-file sibling, SDK file-access export, and installed @openclaw/fs-safe regular-file preflight/nonblocking descriptor/identity/cleanup implementation
- Tests: OPENCLAW_VITEST_RUNTIME=node OPENCLAW_VITEST_MAX_WORKERS=1 node scripts/run-vitest.mjs extensions/openshell/src/worker-cli.test.ts; 5 passed, exit 0 (measured cost: Existing five tests retained; empty/oversized/directory admission assertions folded into existing readiness/stdin case, net new test count 0 and no FIFO writer/timer fixture. Vitest 158.75s, 91% transform)
- Not tested: A real OpenShell daemon, Docker sandbox, successful broker attachment, node startup or model turn; transport fixture intentionally refuses attachment. No native Windows/macOS, installed-release or upgrade claim

Scoped tsgo, typed oxlint, oxfmt, git diff --check and sourcePerformance build exit 0. Test-line6319812/ceiling6351443, mock-factory6447 and timeout-race104files/190sites guards pass. Full author diff simplify/test audit completed; no independent local review claimed. Two files; production +15/-14, tests +11/-0, no generated or lock files. Net production growth of one line replaces unsafe open/stat/read/close with the existing SDK reader and retains actionable input-error context.

