Closes #180756.

## What Problem This Solves

Operators cannot find an earlier error or identifier in the Web terminal's retained canvas output without manually scrolling or repeating commands.

## User Impact

The active terminal gains Find, match counts, previous/next navigation and a highlighted text preview. Finding a match scrolls the real terminal to its retained row without sending search text to the shell. Search is literal, case-sensitive and limited to individual retained visual rows; navigation or Refresh rescans after new output.

## Why This Change Was Made

Read the active Ghostty buffer directly, including full graphemes and explicitly printed spaces, without keeping another output store or changing retention/protocol. A floating control preserves PTY geometry and native selection/copy ownership. Each tab switch retires the search view.

