issues.body:
### Description

The `<>` icon at the start of each tool-call row is clipped on its left edge — the left tip of `<` gets cut by the container edge. Subtle but consistent; more obvious at larger font scale / zoom.

### Environment

- QwenPaw 2.2.2.post1
- Console prebuilt assets (`v1Adapter-*.css`)
- Chrome 152 / Windows

### Steps to reproduce

1. Open the console chat
2. Trigger any tool call (e.g. `execute_shell_command`)
3. Look at the `<>` icon at the leading edge of the tool-call row

### Root cause

The container class `.toolCards-module__toolCallContainer__<hash>` (a CSS module coming from `@agentscope-ai/chat`, surfaced in the console's `v1Adapter` bundle) is declared as:

```
.toolCards-module__toolCallContainer__<hash> {
  width: 100%;
  min-width: 0;
  max-width: 100%;
}
```

No horizontal padding, so the leading icon sits flush against the container's left edge and the leftmost stroke gets clipped.

This rule was introduced by #6677 ("prevent long tool commands from overflowing chat"), which correctly added the width constraints — padding was simply not part of that fix.

### Suggested fix

Add horizontal padding **together with** `box-sizing: border-box`:

```
.toolCards-module__toolCallContainer__<hash> {
  width: 100%;
  min-width: 0;
  max-width: 100%;
  padding: 0 2px;
  box-sizing: border-box;
}
```

`box-sizing` is required here: this stylesheet has no global `*{box-sizing:border-box}` reset, so `width:100%` plus padding would otherwise overflow by 4px and introduce a horizontal scrollbar.

If changing `@agentscope-ai/chat` directly isn't desired, a small override in the console layer works equally well.

### Verification

Applied exactly this rule to the built CSS and reloaded — clipping gone, no layout shift, no overflow.

Happy to open a PR if you'd prefer the override to live on the console side.

